    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/susqu/faculty/jobs/5451814/assistant-professor-of-chemistry": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry Location Selinsgrove, PA Job Type Faculty - Full-Time Benefits Eligible Job Number 0000270 Division School of Natural & Social Sciences Department Chemistry Opening Date 08/18/2026 FLSA Exempt Hours per week Variable Number of months 9 Description Benefits Job Summary The Department of Chemistry at Susquehanna University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in analytical chemistry to start in August 2027. Specific Responsibilities Primary teaching duties will include courses in the department’s introductory sequence (General Chemistry, Methods of Chemical Analysis), plus a special topics course in the candidate’s area of expertise. In addition, the opportunity exists to participate in the university’s First Year Seminar program. The successful candidate is also expected to develop a research program in analytical or bioanalytical chemistry that has significant undergraduate student involvement. Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. in Chemistry is required, and college-level teaching experience and/or postdoctoral research experience is strongly preferred. Preference will also be given to candidates who have a background in chromatography (HPLC, LC/MS). The successful candidate will demonstrate strong evidence for the potential to provide excellence in undergraduate teaching and mentoring. Additional Information for Applicant Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, a statement of research plans including instrumentation needs and a description of how undergraduate students will be involved, and the names and contact information of three references online. Any inquiries should be sent to the Department Head, Dr. Swarna Basu, basu@susqu.edu . For information about the Department and its facilities, please visit https://www.susqu.edu/academics/majors-and-minors/department-of-chemistry . Review of applications will begin on October 5, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Susquehanna University does not provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require employer sponsorship for employment authorization. We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time employees, designed to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance. Our offerings include medical, dental, and vision insurance; retirement savings plans; flexible spending accounts; life and long-term disability insurance; and generous paid time off for holidays, vacation, and sick leave. Employer Susquehanna University Address 514 University Ave Selinsgrove, Pennsylvania, 17870 Phone 5703724024 Website susqu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/susqu/faculty/jobs/5452653/assistant-professor-of-criminal-justice": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice Location Selinsgrove, PA Job Type Faculty - Full-Time Benefits Eligible Job Number 0000274 Division School of Natural & Social Sciences Department Political Science Opening Date 08/18/2026 FLSA Exempt Hours per week Variable Number of months 9 Description Benefits Job Summary Susquehanna University invites applications for a tenure track position at the rank of Assistant Professor to start in August 2027. Specific Responsibilities The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching introductory courses, methodological courses, and advanced topics courses in criminal justice and helping to build the relatively new criminal justice program at SU. Susquehanna University strongly values faculty-student collaborative research and mentoring of students for practica, internships, and admission to graduate programs. Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in criminology and/or criminal justice is required. All specializations (for example, but not limited to, administration and leadership, corrections, rehabilitation, recidivism, courts, juvenile crime, and research methods) will be considered. Demonstrated success or evidence of potential to excel in teaching and advising undergraduates is essential, as is ongoing scholarly productivity and institutional service. Additional Information for Applicant Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching objectives and research interests, and the names and contact information of three references online . Any inquiries should be sent to the search chair, Carol Chen, at chenx@susqu.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 9, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants requiring visa sponsorship are welcome to apply if they are currently maintaining lawful status in the United States and will maintain such lawful status in the United States through the start of the appointment in August 2027. At this time, we are unable to consider candidates who do not have current lawful status in the U.S. We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time employees, designed to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance. Our offerings include medical, dental, and vision insurance; retirement savings plans; flexible spending accounts; life and long-term disability insurance; and generous paid time off for holidays, vacation, and sick leave. Employer Susquehanna University Address 514 University Ave Selinsgrove, Pennsylvania, 17870 Phone 5703724024 Website susqu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/susqu/faculty/jobs/5499276/assistant-track-and-field-cross-country-coach": {
      "title": "Assistant Track and Field & Cross Country Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Track and Field & Cross Country Coach Location Selinsgrove, PA Job Type Faculty - Full-Time Benefits Eligible Job Number 0000300 Division Provost Department Athletics Opening Date 09/29/2026 Closing Date 10/29/2026 11:59 PM Eastern FLSA Determined by Position Hours per week 40 Number of months 12 Description Benefits Job Summary The primary responsibility of this position is to instruct and develop student-athletes in alignment with the university’s academic mission. The assistant coach supports the head coach in administering various aspects of the athletic program. Ideal for individuals passionate about athletics, this role offers hands-on experience and does not require prior coaching experience. Duties may be required before, during, and after the season, as determined by the head coach. This position is classified as exempt under FLSA regulations. Specific Responsibilities Specific Responsibilities Coaching/Teaching (80%) Instruct student athletes in the rules, techniques, and strategies of the sport during practices and competitive events. Provide direct instruction, feedback, and mentorship to enhance athletic performance, sportsmanship, and academic growth. Promote the physical and mental well-being of all student athletes. Secondary Duties (20%) At the discretion of the head coach, the assistant coach may perform a limited range of non-instructional duties. These duties are clearly secondary and comprise only a small portion of the overall role, ensuring that the primary focus remains on the direct instruction and development of student athletes. Secondary duties could include: Provide game day support for other athletic programs as assigned, which may include logistical assistance, bench support, or event coordination. Assist with the development and implementation of both off-campus and on-campus recruiting strategies to identify and attract qualified student athletes who demonstrate academic and athletic potential. Support the planning and execution of organized practices, training sessions, and game strategies. Participate in fundraising activities, promotional events, speaking engagements, and alumni outreach as approved by the program leadership. Minimum Qualifications Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree with no experience; or three (3) years of relevant playing and/or coaching experience. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities Comprehensive knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations with the ability to maintain compliance and report potential concerns promptly. Strong coaching and instructional skills with the ability to communicate concepts clearly and effectively. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously. Ability to advise, motivate, and mentor student-athletes while fostering an inclusive and supportive team culture. Demonstrated ability to assess developmental needs and provide targeted coaching to improve individual and team performance. Additional Information for Applicant Additional Requirements Must possess a valid driver’s license and qualify under the university’s insurance program to operate university or leased vehicles. CPR, AED and First Aid certification required. This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) under the Clery Act. The coach must complete annual CSA training and report any Clery Act crimes disclosed to them. Physical Demands Ability to remain in a stationary position (e.g., sitting or standing) and move about athletic facilities or campus grounds as needed to perform coaching duties. Ability to engage in practice sessions, game-day activities, and occasional event setup, including lifting or moving equipment and materials up to 50 pounds with or without reasonable accommodation. Ability to communicate effectively in both one-on-one and group settings, including giving verbal instructions and providing feedback to student-athletes. Ability to travel regularly and work indoors and outdoors in a variety of weather conditions. Ability to sustain the physical engagement required to actively coach during practices and competitions, including demonstrating techniques, providing on-field or on-court feedback, and participating in team movement as needed. Susquehanna University does not provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require employer sponsorship for employment authorization. We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time employees, designed to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance. Our offerings include medical, dental, and vision insurance; retirement savings plans; flexible spending accounts; life and long-term disability insurance; and generous paid time off for holidays, vacation, and sick leave. Employer Susquehanna University Address 514 University Ave Selinsgrove, Pennsylvania, 17870 Phone 5703724024 Website susqu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/susqu/faculty/jobs/5479265/postdoctoral-scientist": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scientist",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scientist Location Selinsgrove, PA Job Type Faculty - Full-Time Benefits Eligible Job Number 0000291 Division School of Natural & Social Sciences Department Biology Opening Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date 10/23/2026 11:59 PM Eastern FLSA Exempt Hours per week 40 Number of months 12 Description Benefits Job Summary Susquehanna University seeks a highly motivated Postdoctoral Scientist for a two-year position supported by a collaborative National Science Foundation grant. The successful candidate will join the P-MixSwitch project, a collaboration between Susquehanna University and the University of Arizona, investigating the physiological and genetic mechanisms that enable small marine mixoplankton to switch between photosynthetic and predatory lifestyles. The Postdoctoral Scientist will work with investigators and research personnel at both institutions in an interdisciplinary research environment integrating microbial ecology, physiology, molecular biology, and bioinformatics. The position will involve laboratory experiments, molecular and transcriptomic analyses, bioinformatics, manuscript preparation, conference presentations, and mentoring undergraduate researchers. This position is defined as an exempt position under FLSA regulations. Specific Responsibilities Collaborate with researchers at Susquehanna University and the University of Arizona. Spend approximately one to two months per year in Tucson, Arizona, as part of the collaborative research effort. Assist in conducting laboratory experiments with algal cultures. Perform RNA extractions and prepare samples for transcriptomic analyses. Analyze transcriptomic datasets using bioinformatics approaches. Contribute to manuscript preparation and presentation of research findings at scientific conferences. Assist in mentoring undergraduate researchers. Minimum Qualifications Education Ph.D. in Biology, Microbial Ecology, Biological Oceanography, Molecular Biology, Genomics, or a related field required. Experience Experience with molecular biology techniques and/or microbial culturing is required. Experience with transcriptomics, RNA sequencing, and/or bioinformatics is preferred. Experience with data analysis in R, Python, or related platforms preferred. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities Knowledge of microbial ecology, phytoplankton, or protist biology. Strong quantitative and analytical skills. Ability to conduct research independently and collaboratively. Ability to communicate clearly and effectively in written and verbal formats. Ability to work effectively with researchers and research personnel across institutions and disciplines. Additional Information for Applicant Additional Requirements NSF Research Security Training certification is required. Candidates who do not currently hold this certification must complete the training prior to the start of the position. About the P-MixSwitch Project Mixoplankton are ecologically important eukaryotic microorganisms that acquire energy and nutrients through both photosynthesis (phototrophy) and prey consumption (phagotrophy). This dual nutritional strategy allows mixoplankton to play a critical role in global carbon and nutrient cycling. However, the environmental and cellular factors that regulate transitions between phototrophic and phagotrophic modes remain poorly understood. The P-MixSwitch project seeks to uncover the mechanisms underlying this metabolic flexibility by tracking carbon and phosphorus fluxes through nutrient uptake, photosynthetic carbon fixation, and phagotrophic ingestion of prey. Using physiological, molecular, and transcriptomic approaches, the project will characterize the cellular and subcellular changes associated with trophic switching in ecologically important prasinophyte mixoplankton. This work will advance understanding of the role of marine mixoplankton in carbon cycling within oligotrophic ocean ecosystems. Research Environment The Charvet Lab at Susquehanna University uses molecular biology and bioinformatics approaches to investigate genes and pathways involved in mixoplankton phagotrophy under varying environmental conditions. As part of the P-MixSwitch project, the Postdoctoral Scientist will participate in collaborative experimental work with the University of Arizona, followed by RNA extraction, transcriptome sequencing, and gene expression analyses of key prasinophyte strains. This is a full-time, two-year postdoctoral appointment funded by the National Science Foundation, with an anticipated start date of January 2027. As a grant-funded position, the salary is established by the grant award and is not negotiable. Applicants must submit a cover letter, CV, and contact information for three references through the online application system. Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Sophie Charvet at charvet@susqu.edu . Susquehanna University does not provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require employer sponsorship for employment authorization. We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time employees, designed to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance. Our offerings include medical, dental, and vision insurance; retirement savings plans; flexible spending accounts; life and long-term disability insurance; and generous paid time off for holidays, vacation, and sick leave. Employer Susquehanna University Address 514 University Ave Selinsgrove, Pennsylvania, 17870 Phone 5703724024 Website susqu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/susqu/faculty/jobs/5512076/visiting-assistant-professor-of-finance": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Finance Location Selinsgrove, PA Job Type Faculty - Full-Time Benefits Eligible Job Number 0000304 Division Sigmund Weis School of Business Department Finance and Analytics Opening Date 10/09/2026 FLSA Exempt Hours per week Varies Number of months 10 Description Benefits Job Summary The Sigmund Weis School of Business (SWSB) of Susquehanna University seeks applicants for the position of Visiting Assistant Professor of Finance. This is a full-time, one-year position beginning in Fall 2027. Undergraduate teaching includes corporate financial management and upper-level finance courses. Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in Finance, Financial Economics, or a related field. Candidates who are ABD with expected completion prior to start date will also be considered. A candidate with a master’s degree and significant professional experience will also be considered. A record that illustrates current (or suggests the potential for) excellent teaching is also required. This candidate will be expected to interact openly and inspire students through their teaching strategies, which demonstrate a high level of organization and communication. Required qualifications include : Ability to teach an introductory corporate finance class to all majors in the SWSB. Ability to teach an upper-level finance class Preferred Qualifications include : Ability to teach upper-level economics, real estate, risk management, or business analytics courses. Additional Information for Applicant Please submit your curriculum vitae/resume, statement of teaching objectives and research interests, and the name, address, e-mail address, and telephone number of three references online. Any inquiries should be sent to Dr. James Pomykalski, pomykalski@susqu.edu , Chair of the Department of Finance and Analytics or Dr. Matt Rousu, rousu@susqu.edu , Dean of the Sigmund Weis School of Business. Review of applications will begin on November 9 th and will continue until the position is filled. Susquehanna University does not provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require employer sponsorship for employment authorization. We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time employees, designed to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance. Our offerings include medical, dental, and vision insurance; retirement savings plans; flexible spending accounts; life and long-term disability insurance; and generous paid time off for holidays, vacation, and sick leave. Employer Susquehanna University Address 514 University Ave Selinsgrove, Pennsylvania, 17870 Phone 5703724024 Website susqu.edu Apply"
    }
